# Accepted risk, tracked in TODOS.md ("Remove .trivyignore entry for
# CVE-2026-56854") -- remove this line once either is true:
#   1. paketo-buildpacks/npm-install bumps golang.org/x/crypto to >=0.55.0
#      (confirmed still pinned at 0.54.0 on its main branch as of this
#      writing -- no fix released yet, no upstream issue filed either),
#   2. or this expiry passes, forcing a re-check rather than silently
#      accepting the risk indefinitely.
# The vulnerable binary is npm-install's own exec.d symlink-setup helper
# (a build-time buildpack tool embedded in the launch layer), not
# cv_frontend's or toolbox's code -- CVE-2026-56854 is an SSH
# auth-bypass in golang.org/x/crypto/ssh; that helper never establishes
# an SSH connection.
CVE-2026-56854 exp:2026-12-04

# Accepted risk, tracked in TODOS.md ("Remove .trivyignore entry for
# CVE-2026-59873") -- remove this line once either is true:
#   1. paketo-buildpacks/node-engine's builder-jammy-base indexes Node
#      >=24.20.0 (confirmed live: Node 24.20.0 already bundles npm 11.19.0
#      -> tar 7.5.19, the fix -- but builder-jammy-base's own Node index
#      tops out at 24.19.0; `pack build --env BP_NODE_VERSION=24.20.0`
#      fails outright: "no compatible versions... Supported versions are:
#      [...24.18.1, 24.19.0, 26.6.0...]". The fix exists upstream, this
#      builder image just hasn't re-baked to include it yet.),
#   2. or this expiry passes, forcing a re-check.
# The vulnerable tar is bundled inside Node 24.19.0's own npm installation
# (layers/paketo-buildpacks_node-engine/node/lib/node_modules/npm/
# node_modules/tar) -- not cv_frontend's dependency tree (confirmed: it
# has no `tar` entry anywhere in its own package-lock.json). npm is never
# invoked at runtime by this app (`node --import remix/node-tsx
# server.ts`, no npm subprocess), so the DoS-via-crafted-gzip vector needs
# something to feed it attacker-controlled archive data at runtime, which
# doesn't happen here.
CVE-2026-59873 exp:2026-12-04
